# The pages under docs/viz/ are committed build output, pinned byte-for-byte by
# DocsPagesGoldenTest against the generator that produced them. Git's autocrlf would hand a
# Windows checkout CRLF line endings, and every one of those goldens would fail on a student's
# first `mvn test` — a broken build on first contact, in a repo whose whole point is being
# approachable. Normalising to LF in the working tree keeps the bytes the generator emitted.
*.html text eol=lf

# Not load-bearing, just consistency: keep the rest of the tree on one line ending so a
# cross-platform checkout produces no spurious whole-file diffs. (README.md is also read by a
# test, so it benefits from the same determinism, if less sharply than the goldens do.)
*.md text eol=lf
*.java text eol=lf
